From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gsfork <gsfork@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:01:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] S04: overridable default app template

Why:         GameStudio Editor opens in its IDE shell (the GameStudio app template) without
             launcher arguments; a saved preference cannot do this (readfile.cc clears it).
             `--app-template default` still starts plain Blender.
Hook-for:    editor/native/CMakeLists.txt (WM_DEFAULT_APP_TEMPLATE)
Upstream:    candidate (default template for distributions)
Test:        editor/tests/shell test_template_is_active
Remove-when: upstream supports a build-time default template
---
 source/blender/windowmanager/intern/wm_files.cc | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/blender/windowmanager/intern/wm_files.cc b/source/blender/windowmanager/intern/wm_files.cc
index 39c8fa5df124a97b3dcdd390233af177fc048132..ba6d68bf8b4ddc126a1cd457981d3cce151ddd50 100644
--- a/source/blender/windowmanager/intern/wm_files.cc
+++ b/source/blender/windowmanager/intern/wm_files.cc
@@ -1156,10 +1156,15 @@ bool WM_file_read(bContext *C,
   return success;
 }
 
+/* Distributions of Blender can start in their own app template by default. */
+#ifndef WM_DEFAULT_APP_TEMPLATE
+#  define WM_DEFAULT_APP_TEMPLATE ""
+#endif
+
 static struct {
   char app_template[64];
   bool override;
-} wm_init_state_app_template = {{0}};
+} wm_init_state_app_template = {WM_DEFAULT_APP_TEMPLATE, sizeof(WM_DEFAULT_APP_TEMPLATE) > 1};
 
 void WM_init_state_app_template_set(const char *app_template)
 {
